P8-mariadb-001 patch (outside write scope: xtask/). Rationale: the allowlist-lock gate's independent generator
(xtask/src/allowlist.rs) knew only sqlite/postgres/redis/valkey and its Deny::hit sent every unknown family to the
RESP table, so apps/notes/allowlist.notes-mariadb.lock (committed by this unit) fails `--check` with "bad family
line". This patch adds `mariadb` to FAMILIES, reads the MARIADB_DENY table from crates/monban-data-ir/src/ir.rs
(fail closed if missing), gives Deny::hit explicit arms (redis|valkey -> RESP, mariadb -> MARIADB; any other family
denies every word instead of silently using RESP), and mirrors lock.rs native_words for the MariaDB upsert skeleton
(ODKU, or INSERT .. SELECT .. FROM DUAL WHERE NOT EXISTS when nothing is set; never ON CONFLICT DO, since DO is
denied on MariaDB). No existing check is weakened: every prior mutant and control is unchanged. New self-test
mutants (all caught on kamrui): deny-mariadb-{replace,handler,ignore,call}, mariadb-skeleton-checked (a denylist
source that also denies DUPLICATE refuses the fixture upsert), mariadb-decl-as-postgres, denylist-mariadb-table-missing,
deny-unknown-family-fails-closed; positive controls gain FIX_MY and the HANDLER/DO denylist probes.
Verified on kamrui with the patch applied to a copy of p8/mariadb-001: `cargo xtask allowlist-lock --check` ->
ALLOWLIST-LOCK: PASS (6 locks, 38 entries ...); `--self-test` -> PASS (40/40 mutants caught ...); `--emit
apps/notes/allowlist.notes-mariadb.decl` byte-identical to the committed lock; `cargo test -p xtask allowlist` 2 passed.
Apply with: git apply units/phase-8/patches/P8-mariadb-001.patch

